WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.160
In Lagos, two software developers kept hearing the same complaint from small businesses.

2
00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:10.142
Taking payments online was slow,

3
00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:14.602
expensive, and built for companies much larger than theirs.

4
00:00:14.882 --> 00:00:18.062
Every failed transaction cost a merchant trust.

5
00:00:19.141 --> 00:00:21.301
So they built a simpler checkout.

6
00:00:21.761 --> 00:00:23.541
One integration, one dashboard,

7
00:00:23.841 --> 00:00:25.861
and money that arrived where it was needed.

8
00:00:26.831 --> 00:00:27.911
The market was crowded.

9
00:00:28.731 --> 00:00:30.231
Trust was scarce.

10
00:00:30.671 --> 00:00:33.091
And every merchant wanted proof before switching.

11
00:00:33.151 --> 00:00:34.291
Growth was possible,

12
00:00:34.691 --> 00:00:37.751
but only if the product worked every single day.

13
00:00:38.811 --> 00:00:39.911
Then the numbers moved.

14
00:00:40.591 --> 00:00:42.791
Developers adopted it, investors noticed,

15
00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:48.371
and in 2020 Stripe acquired Paystack for about two hundred million dollars.

16
00:00:48.431 --> 00:00:52.031
It was one of the largest exits in Nigerian tech at the time.

17
00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:55.583
The lesson is not that payments are glamorous.

18
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:56.703
It is that a clear,

19
00:00:56.763 --> 00:00:59.763
useful tool can travel farther than a loud idea.

20
00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:04.910
Small problems, solved properly, can build something the whole world uses.

